# Minimal manual production reference. The one-click installer writes the real
# protected file to C:\Algentra\secrets\core-api.env and generates secrets.
# APP_ENV, HTTP_ADDR, ADMIN_USERNAME, and COOKIE_SECURE use secure service
# defaults in start-core-api.ps1/config.go and do not need to be repeated here.
DATABASE_URL=

# APP_SECRET_KEY is generated on first start and stored in the protected local
# integration-secrets/app-secret.json file. A legacy value is migrated once.

# For a manual first start on an empty database only, set ADMIN_PASSWORD once;
# after the admin hash is created, it can be removed. The installer generates it.
# Gemini is configured from the admin dashboard and stored locally.
# EA API key is generated at first start and shown under Dashboard > Settings.
# Telegram API ID/hash and optional bot credentials are stored in the
# protected integration-secrets/telegram.json file by the one-click installer.
# Legacy TELEGRAM_* environment values are migrated there on the next install.
# The one-click installer stores payment, Midtrans, and SMTP configuration in
# backend/data/integration-secrets/optional-integrations.json, not this file.
# Legacy payment/EMAIL_SMTP_* environment values are migrated to that file.
# For a manual production launch, the backend still accepts these variables:
# PAYMENT_BANK_NAME / PAYMENT_NUMBER / PAYMENT_NAME
# MIDTRANS_SERVER_KEY / MIDTRANS_MERCHANT_ID / MIDTRANS_IS_PRODUCTION / MIDTRANS_NOTIFICATION_URL
# EMAIL_SMTP_HOST / EMAIL_SMTP_PORT / EMAIL_SMTP_USERNAME / EMAIL_SMTP_PASSWORD / EMAIL_FROM / EMAIL_SMTP_STARTTLS
